-a97cf4629a11&q;,&q;language&q;:&q;&q;,&q;value&q;:&q;&l;div class=\&q;ExternalClass3845D77A7F2F41EEA317C3C99D5A028C\&q;&g;&l;p&g;Copyright&a;#58; FAO, ILC and&a;#160;CIRAD&a;#160;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;Logo&a;#58; FAO, ILC and CIRAD logos on the top FAO first followed up by ILC and CIRAD&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;AU&a;#58; FAO, ILC and CIRAD (individual authors if the publication falls under Tier 2.&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;PU&a;#58; FAO.ILC and CIRAD&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;FAO can sell&a;#58; yes&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;FAO doi&a;#58; yes&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&l;p&g;Title&a;#58; Please note that the title of the publication should be changed to&a;#160;&s;Status of..&s; from the &a;quot;State of..&a;quot; as the&a;#160;&s;State of...&s; is reserved only for the FAO Flagship publications.&a;#160;&l;br&g;&l;/p&g;&l;div class=\&q;x_elementToProof\&q; data-olk-copy-source=\&q;MessageBody\&q; style=\&q;border&a;#58;0px;font-style&a;#58;inherit;font-variant&a;#58;inherit;font-weight&a;#58;inherit;font-stretch&a;#58;inherit;font-size&a;#58;11pt;line-height&a;#58;inherit;font-family&a;#58;aptos, aptos_embeddedfont, aptos_msfontservice, calibri, helvetica, sans-serif, serif, emojifont;font-size-adjust&a;#58;inherit;font-feature-settings&a;#58;inherit;margin&a;#58;0px;padding&a;#58;0px;vertical-align&a;#58;baseline;color&a;#58;#000000;direction&a;#58;ltr;\&q;&g;&a;#160;All the ones that are not flagships may use&a;#160;&l;em&g;Status of&l;/em&g;, see below&a;#160;some recent examples for your information. With regard to the title in the copublishing agreement, it says provisionally entitled, and it should not be an issue for FAO to change the title without informing the copublishers. But if ESP wishes to sign an addendum, let us know and we can send an addendum to the copublishers.&l;br&g;&l;/div&g;&l;div class=\&q;x_elementToProof\&q; style=\&q;border&a;#58;0px;font-style&a;#58;inherit;font-variant&a;#58;inherit;font-weight&a;#58;inherit;font-stretch&a;#58;inherit;font-size&a;#58;11pt;line-height&a;#58;1.